WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.330
Here's how PadForge keeps itself up to date, and where you remove its drivers.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.610
You're hearing a generated voice.

3
00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:11.815
Open Settings, and find the Updates card.

4
00:00:12.385 --> 00:00:16.795
PadForge checks GitHub 20 seconds after it starts, then every 12 hours.

5
00:00:18.443 --> 00:00:20.493
Click Check Now to look right away.

6
00:00:21.103 --> 00:00:22.433
When a newer version is out,

7
00:00:22.723 --> 00:00:25.733
Install and Restart puts it in place, and starts it again.

8
00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:30.299
Or turn on Install Updates Automatically,

9
00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:33.659
and a new version goes in the next time PadForge starts.

10
00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.104
Further down are the driver cards.

11
00:00:40.574 --> 00:00:46.544
Uninstall removes a driver, HIDMaestro and BthPS3 included.

12
00:00:47.274 --> 00:00:50.004
PadForge installs them again when something needs them.

13
00:00:52.325 --> 00:00:54.855
Find more guides at padforge.org.
